      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think this change is safe? All *writes* occur on the handler, yes, but not all reads - in particular:\n- shouldHonorSystemThresholds\n- getConsolidatedSignalThresholds\n\nIt\u0027s still possible to get a concurrency error when those reader methods are looping over the list (or using a stream) at the same time that the handler calls .add/.remove.\n\nIn fact, I think we need to *add* synchronization to shouldHonorSystemThresholds to avoid issues.",
